---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Browse - Harbor Legal Independent Index" description="Browse bills and court rulings across every US jurisdiction. Filter by state, area of law, or court — or search for something specific." activeNav="browse">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Browse</p>
      <h1>Start anywhere. The whole picture is already here.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Pick a state, a court, or an area of law and see everything in motion. You don't need to
        know what you're looking for to get value from the index — but when you do have something
        specific in mind, search is there.
      </p>
      <div class="tag-row">
        <span class="tag">All 50 states</span>
        <span class="tag">Congress</span>
        <span class="tag">Federal circuits</span>
        <span class="tag">Supreme Court</span>
        <span class="tag">Areas of law</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="surface">
          <div class="card-label">By jurisdiction</div>
          <div class="card-value">State or federal</div>
          <p class="card-copy">
            Choose any state or the federal level and see what's been introduced, what's moved,
            and what's been signed into law this session — updated daily from official legislative
            sources.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="surface">
          <div class="card-label">By topic</div>
          <div class="card-value">Area of law</div>
          <p class="card-copy">
            Follow housing, privacy, labor, firearms, or any major legal domain across every
            jurisdiction at once. See the full scope of what's moving without manually checking
            each state.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="surface">
          <div class="card-label">By court</div>
          <div class="card-value">Rulings that matter</div>
          <p class="card-copy">
            Browse federal appeals circuits and Supreme Court opinions filtered to decisions that
            shift how existing law is interpreted — and see which active bills they connect to.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">How the index is organized</p>
          <h2>What you can navigate without searching</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="roadmap-grid">
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Bills</div>
          <h3>Introduction through enactment</h3>
          <p>Every bill is tracked from introduction through committee, chamber passage, and signing. Filter by stage to see what's active, what stalled, and what became law.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Courts</div>
          <h3>Opinions and orders</h3>
          <p>Circuit court opinions, SCOTUS decisions, cert grants, and orders — with enough context to understand what changed and which statutes or pending bills are affected.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Areas of law</div>
          <h3>Cross-jurisdiction topics</h3>
          <p>A single view across all states and federal activity for a given legal domain. See the full legislative and court picture for a topic without constructing it yourself.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Connections</div>
          <h3>Bills and rulings together</h3>
          <p>When a court ruling reshapes how a statute is read, the affected bills surface alongside it. When a bill passes that codifies a recent ruling, the link is there.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Recency</div>
          <h3>What moved this week</h3>
          <p>A feed of recent activity across the whole index — bills that advanced, opinions that dropped, cert grants that signal a coming shift. No digging required.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Search</div>
          <h3>When you need something specific</h3>
          <p>Full-text search across bills, opinions, and summaries when you already know what you're looking for — a bill number, a case name, a statutory term, a keyword.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="surface">
        <p class="eyebrow">Coming next</p>
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 0.6rem">Alerts and saved views</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin:0; max-width:unset">
          Once the index is stable, the next layer is personalization: follow a bill, watch a
          jurisdiction, subscribe to an area of law. Get notified when something you care about
          moves, without having to check back manually.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
